# English Coach

Personal, local-first English speaking coach. Simplicity, speed, useful feedback, and privacy outrank features.

- Stay on the current phase in `docs/progress.md`. Do not implement later phases early.
- Use one relevant skill from `.cursor/skills/`. Load only the docs that skill lists.
- Application logic owns session state, learner profile, focus, topics, and measurements. The LLM only converses, corrects, and writes exercises.
- One LLM call per speaking turn. Keep replies short.
- Do not invent pronunciation or proficiency percentages. Say when a measurement is approximate.
- No paid APIs, accounts, or cloud storage in the core path.
- Keep Whisper and Ollama weights under the repo `.models` folder, on the drive that has free space. Do not assume a `D:` drive.
- Correct at most one or two problems per turn.

## Commits

Use a Conventional Commit subject: `type: why this change exists`.

- `feat` — someone can use a new behavior
- `fix` — a broken behavior works again
- `docs` — documentation only
- `test` — tests
- `refactor` — structure change with the same behavior
- `perf` — a measured speed or memory improvement
- `chore` — skills, tooling, or repo maintenance

Keep one phase or one fix in each commit. Do not mix unrelated work.
